<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cangrande I della Scala</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1291">1291</a>–<a href="/years/1329">1329</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cangrande I della Scala was lord of Verona from 1311 to 1329 and the most powerful of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scaliger">Scaliger</a> family. Imperial vicar and Ghibelline leader, he conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vicenza">Vicenza</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a> and Treviso, making Verona the leading power of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. He sheltered the exiled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dante-alighieri">Dante</a>, who dedicated the Paradiso to him, and died days after taking Treviso.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cangrande-i-della-scala.jpg" alt="Cangrande I della Scala" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sailko · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maestro_dell%27arca_di_mastino_II,_statua_a_cavallo_di_cangrande_della_scala,_1340_ca._03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
